{
  "_help": [
    "HardwareOne multi-device registry. Copy to ~/.openclaw/hardwareone.devices.json (host-only, chmod 600).",
    "When this file exists the gateway uses it; otherwise it falls back to a single device in hardwareone.env.",
    "Device names are free identifiers (NOT rooms) - a device's room/location/purpose lives on the device",
    "(espnowroom / espnowzone / espnowtags) and in the agent's memory note, never here.",
    "role: master | worker | backup. A DIRECT master is an HTTP entry point the agent talks to AND the",
    "jumping-off point for the mesh. You may configure SEVERAL co-equal direct masters (each controllable",
    "by name); 'default' picks which one bare/un-targeted commands use. If you omit 'default' with 2+ masters",
    "the gateway auto-picks the first by name (ASCII order, so uppercase sorts before lowercase) and notes",
    "it. A 'backup' (also direct) becomes the",
    "default if the master is down.",
    "Two co-equal HTTP endpoints (no shared mesh)? Give BOTH a url and role:master, e.g.:",
    "  \"node-a\": {\"url\":\"192.0.2.42\",\"role\":\"master\",\"user\":\"admin\",\"pass\":\"...\"},",
    "  \"node-c\": {\"url\":\"192.0.2.77\",\"role\":\"master\",\"user\":\"admin\",\"pass\":\"...\"}",
    "and set \"default\" to the one bare commands should use; reach the other by name.",
    "Credentials: each DIRECT device needs its own url + user + pass. If ALL your devices truly share one",
    "login you can move user/pass up into 'defaults'; otherwise keep them per device (as below).",
    "via: \"mesh\" marks a device with NO direct HTTP - it is reached by relaying espnowremote through the",
    "master. It still needs user + pass (an account ON THE PEER) so the gateway can run espnowremote for you;",
    "it needs NO url. It shows up as access:mesh and the agent addresses it by name like any device. NOTE:",
    "espnowremote splits arguments on spaces, so a mesh device's user/pass must be space-free.",
    "description (optional, any device): a short operator note about that device's HARDWARE/SOFTWARE setup",
    "- e.g. 'ESP32-S3, thermal camera + mic + on-device LLM' or 'battery ToF node, mesh-only'. It is shown",
    "to the agent via hardwareone_devices (names/roles/descriptions are the ONLY things the agent sees -",
    "never url/user/pass). Room/location/purpose still live on the device + memory note, NOT here.",
    "Transport: prefer an explicit https:// URL. Explicit https:// and http:// URLs are pinned.",
    "A bare host uses HTTPS; allowHttp:true permits HTTP only after HTTPS connection refusal.",
    "allowHttp must be set on the individual device; defaults.allowHttp is ignored.",
    "Plain HTTP is for a trusted, isolated LAN. Prefer an explicit http:// URL when it is intentional.",
    "For self-signed HTTPS, prefer cacert:'/host/path/device-ca.pem' (the device cert SAN must match the URL).",
    "allowSelfSigned:true disables certificate verification and is a trusted-LAN-only alternative.",
    "allowHttp and allowSelfSigned are separate: neither one implies or enables the other.",
    "Advanced optional per-device fields: connectTimeout, timeout, timeoutMedium, timeoutLong, authProbe (seconds / path).",
    "timeout also caps each login request; timeout/timeoutMedium/timeoutLong are the budgets for fast/medium/slow",
    "commands as classed in plugin/command-speeds.js (unset: 30 s / 75 s / 75 s on a direct device).",
    "Lines in this _help array are ignored by the parser - delete them or keep them, your choice."
  ],
  "default": "node-a",
  "defaults": { "allowSelfSigned": false },
  "devices": {
    "node-a": { "url": "https://192.0.2.42", "role": "master", "user": "admin", "pass": "replace-with-device-password", "cacert": "/absolute/path/to/node-a-ca.pem", "description": "ESP32-S3 - thermal camera, mic, on-device LLM" },
    "node-b": { "role": "worker", "via": "mesh", "user": "node-b", "pass": "replace-with-device-password", "description": "battery ToF sensor node, mesh-only" }
  }
}
